# polygon.technology — crawler policy.
#
# The whole site is open to crawlers. We ALSO explicitly welcome the major
# AI / LLM crawlers (answer engines and training/RAG fetchers) so Polygon
# content is eligible to surface in generative search — a deliberate
# generative-engine-optimization stance for launch, not the default (several
# of these bots are widely blocked). Each is named with an explicit allow so
# the intent is unambiguous and easy to revisit per-bot later.
#
# /401 and /cdn-cgi/ stay disallowed, matching the current live site: /401 is
# an auth-error page with nothing worth indexing, and /cdn-cgi/ is
# Cloudflare's own internal path, never a real site route. /search is also
# disallowed: it's a bare query surface (?q=<anything>), not content of its
# own, and letting it be crawled/indexed lets spam backlinks with arbitrary
# query strings get indexed and attributed under this domain.
#
# The sitemap lists every public route (the internal /gallery review surface
# is deliberately excluded — see astro.config.mjs).

User-agent: *
Allow: /
Disallow: /401
Disallow: /cdn-cgi/
Disallow: /search

